        "original_id": "1b13e042-4b9d-5021-896f-0da350b0f6a0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ridley Scott, Elmer Clifton, D.W. Griffith, Joseph Henabery, Paige Lewis, Eric Garcia\n- Films: Alien, Blade Runner, Gladiator, The Martian, The Birth of a Nation, Intolerance, Matchstick Men\n- Roles: film director, producer, actor, mentor, singer-songwriter, copywriter\n- Places: England, Katy, Texas\n\nFacts:\n- Ridley Scott was born on 30 November 1937 and is an English film director and producer.\n- Elmer Clifton collaborated with D.W. Griffith and appeared in The Birth of a Nation in 1915.\n- Elmer Clifton collaborated with D.W. Griffith and appeared in Intolerance in 1916.\n- In 1917, Elmer Clifton gave up acting to concentrate on work behind the camera, with D.W. Griffith and Joseph Henabery as his mentors.\n- Ridley Scott had his commercial breakthrough with Alien in 1979.\n- Ridley Scott directed Blade Runner in 1982.\n- Matchstick Men is a 2003 British-American black comedy crime film directed by Ridley Scott and based on Eric Garcia's 2002 novel of the same name.\n- Ridley Scott directed Gladiator in 2000, and the film won the Best Picture Oscar.\n- Paige Lewis is a singer-songwriter and copywriter from Katy, Texas, and her work was featured on the soundtrack of Matchstick Men.\n- Ridley Scott directed The Martian in 2015.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
